Z||000006||bHooper||10-19-2001||01:35 PM||||Thanks, guys!<P>Unless you've been out there in this job market, you have no idea how bad things are.  So many people have been let go, that companies can hold out to interview the "right person" with the exact experience.  No more of this, we will take a good person even if he doesn't have the experince stuff.<P>Never mind that I have never found anything I can't do, given the oportunity.<P>And on the bright side, they didn't mention asstek's in the minivan line!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Nashco||10-19-2001||01:46 PM||||Hey, easy on the minivan....I'll drive anything if they're providing it!  Who cares what it is, if you get to drive it as you please without worries?  Seriously...think of the maintenance they get that you don't have to pay for!  Yeah, it would be nice if it were a nicer automobile, but anything free is nice.  Heck, for free, I'd even drive mus..er...nevermind <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Congrats on the new job...oh, and unemployment end and new job at the same time?  Coincidence?  I think not... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever3000||10-19-2001||02:28 PM||||Glad to hear it!  That's some good news.  If I get on dayshift, I'll have to wear a tie also.  In fact our company is having a "mandatory" meeting about dress code crap today and I'm not going.  I'll just show up at my usual time and say I forgot.<P>I always liked Swishers.  Been about a year since I had one however.<BR>||||reg||1
